course: dictionary
lesson: 13602
title: Adverbs that tell how
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An adverb tells you how, when or where something happens. Many adverbs end in -ly. Incorrectly tells you how something was done: in a wrong way, not correctly. «Mia spelt the word incorrectly.» That means she did not spell it right.
explain: Find the action word first, then ask how it was done. «Sam added the numbers incorrectly, so his answer was wrong.» The action is added, and incorrectly says how he added: in a wrong way.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word that fits. Wrongly is a good swap: «Sam added the numbers wrongly» still makes sense, so you have understood incorrectly.
fact: Incorrectly is an adverb, so it tells how something is done.
fact: «Incorrectly» means in a wrong way; not correctly.
fact: The adjective is incorrect: «The answer is incorrect» means the answer is not right.
fact: Maths: «The sum was added incorrectly.» Safety: «A seat belt worn incorrectly does not protect you.» Science: equipment used incorrectly gives wrong results.
fact: A synonym for incorrectly is wrongly.
exercise: «The sum was added incorrectly.» What does incorrectly mean here? | In a neat way | In a quick way | In a loud way | *In a wrong way
exercise: Which word means the same as incorrectly? | *Wrongly | Happily | Carefully | Quickly
exercise: «He wore his seat belt incorrectly.» What does this tell you? | *He did not wear it the right way, so it may not protect him | He wore it very tightly | He wore it in the car park | He wore it every day for years
test: «The scientist used the microscope incorrectly and got wrong results.» Which word tells you how the scientist used it? | microscope | results | *incorrectly | scientist
test: What does «He spelt the word incorrectly» mean? | He spelt it on the board | *He spelt it in a wrong way | He spelt it very fast | He spelt it with a friend
exam: «The shopkeeper counted the change incorrectly.» Which word could replace incorrectly? | cheerfully | loudly | *wrongly | slowly
